{"title":"Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Linear Algebra-2","fileName":"063_Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Linear Algebra-2.html","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Data Science and AI","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The eigen values of the matrix, <img src=\"/media/14849038269ce2443c6514f209adcc8689c30a4b.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> are 1 and 6. For matrix <img src=\"/media/c7054adf4c6ac9d7c92f4843ff1844a08c9144e1.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is the 2 × 2<br />\nidentity matrix and α is a constant. If the eigen values of matrix <em>B</em> are 5 and 10, find the value of α.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>4</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b0ffd8fc6faf1f145e8a5f40c1c5f4f2fb718866.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the given matrix <img src=\"/media/0055ec64be1fd0220f8fa0825fb29df0d22cca48.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> the eigen vectors.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e031e2e1d482fb1e38ff0336fdd4c5c0e5cab210.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3b5b9c62cc1d9110fbbccf46e8e910f32c96bad8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/d8ac963adddf59696f489ed86e94703f613dd218.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3f8282a2af32f32e8fe393bdf2e4f3e189d235ad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c250c6d11918dd685ca26a03d7760f595b486e19.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3d96f3dcc76984810124a35c01e802ed547cc2dd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n</div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For which values of α and β the following simultaneously equations have an infinite number of solution</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c3ef97f9f203847d4a70c035760456d1bfdac837.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> (14, –5)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> (4, –1)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> (1, –4)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> (5, 14)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/06a1b0513155b8dc6fe90eeb2d67da45cc2a4c09.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5e2c572303cbe553f3399085c322a5696e5843ca.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n</div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The eigen value of skew-symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = –<em>A</em>] are purely real.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The eigen value of skew-symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = –<em>A</em>] are purely imaginary or zero.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The eigen value of symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = <em>A</em>] are purely imaginary.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The eigen value of symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = <em>A</em>] are purely real.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, d)<br />\n&bull; The eigen value of symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = <em>A</em>] are purely real.<br />\n&bull; The eigen value of skew-symmetric matrix [<em>A<sup>T</sup></em> = &ndash;<em>A</em>] are either imaginary or zeros.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Let A be a 6 × 6 real matrix whose characteristic polynomial is<br />\n(y – 1)<sup>3</sup> ⋅ (y – 2)<sup>2</sup> ⋅ (y – 3)<sup>1</sup><br />\nLet λ = 2 be one eigen values of <em>A</em>.<br />\nWhich of the following is necessarily true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> λ = 2 have one independent eigen vector.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Rank of the matrix ≤ 3.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Geometric multiplicity of λ = 2 is 2.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c879fe6d0017b0c9f48c5eb66c28f08d72662fa9.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8b94088c0cc1ea7d245f8de620ce6e210a353db3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If <em>A</em> is a 6 × 6 matrix with det(<em>A</em>) = –1<br />\nDefine matrix <em>B</em> = 2<em>A</em><sup>–1</sup> (–<em>A<sup>T</sup></em>)<br />\nDeterminant of det(<em>B</em>) = ?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"64","high":"64"},"solution":"<p>64</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/86029ca812dfe3b9a0dcbae9cdc4482f3ead042f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider <em>A</em><sub><em>n</em> × <em>m</em></sub> and <em>B</em><sub><em>m</em> × <em>n</em></sub> matrices <em>n</em> < <em>m</em>.<br />\nWhich of the following is/are true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>AB</em> have atmost n linearly independent vectors.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <em>BA</em> can be invertible, having non-zero determinant.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>BA</em> have greater then n non-zero eigen values.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both <em>AB</em> and <em>BA</em> have equal non-zero eigen values.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, d)<br />\n&there4; <em>AB</em> and BA have same non-zero eigen values.<br />\n&there4; <em>AB</em> have rank atmost <em>n</em>, so <em>n</em> LI vectors possible.<br />\n&there4; <em>BA</em> have greater than equal two (<em>m</em> &ndash; <em>n</em>) zero eigen values.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider matrix <em>A</em><sub><em>n</em> × <em>n</em></sub> having eigen values λ<sub>1</sub>, λ<sub>2</sub>, ..... λ<em><sub>n</sub></em>.<br />\nWhich of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3e73768f005f3296f5e11cb1a507642e34664617.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4c94c0f21d26493fc65f8c91ee23e49023e577ed.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/ba307417a6f1f7a2f4e8a05cb69db3b801d41d52.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> All are true.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b)<br />\n(c) Matrix may have repeated eigen value, which may lead non-diagonalizable matrix.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following matrix:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dfeaad5ff0d0b8c1226d057aa81095e108066b08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which are true regarding matrix <em>A</em>?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Rank of the matrix is 4.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The system <em>AX</em> = 0 has only trivial solution.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The nullity of <em>A</em> is 1.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The maximum number of linearly independent column is 4.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/813cde0ce3d3d34af98f16bad8301d38523245ab.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Let A be a real symmetric 3 × 3 matrix with eigen value 4, λ, λ.<br />\nSuppose det(<em>A</em>) = 16 and trace(<em>A</em>) = 10<br />\nWhat are the possible values of λ.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2, –2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2, 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> –2, 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> No value of λ possible</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6c5352e59602a1428089e97276489aed26174381.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : The product of singular values of n × n matrix is equal to the determinant of the matrix.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : If all singular value of an n × n matrix are non-zero, then the determinant of the matrix is the sum of it’s non-zero singular values.<br />\nWhich of the below is true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following matrix given below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/dfdc39d945ff4bd3f17912914a308fd5b24e8cb7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>Which of the following is true about above matrix ?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> [<em>A</em>]<em><sup>T</sup></em> = [<em>A</em>]<sup>–1</sup></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3650a234db52c8963f4015500c3810269683f6f4.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/ab9184a421fb9f95c55789e35cf91a8982cae0d2.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> All of the above</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/beab1b5264bc50b77ccfa4d438ce26e097c177c0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The given equations are solved by using <em>LU</em>-decomposition method.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5e866c2588a689971947f4c94a7f96929d03129b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>What is the upper triangle matrix value?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4576f600cc636cd95d5ab494381dcbc9dc92bcba.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/25a0ab2c01921b5974cb3e17aec0130a5b5eeb80.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/de03fc819a3fc558b3fc62c21814b0d595ac8653.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of above</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d8926d7774b63187cabdcf11689933b4582a9faf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the singular value decomposition of a real matrix <em>A</em> ∈ <em>R</em><sup><em>n</em> × <em>n</em></sup>, given by <em>A</em> = U Σ <em>V<sup>T</sup></em>.<br />\nS<sub>1</sub> : The matrix <em>A<sup>T</sup>A</em> has an orthonormal set of eigen vectors given by the columns of V.<br />\nS<sub>2</sub> : The diagonal entries of Σ arc the square roots of the non-zero eigen values of <em>A<sup>T</sup>A</em>.<br />\nWhich of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>If <em>u</em> and <em>v</em> are orthogonal vector in the inner product space <em>v</em>, such that \u0001<img src=\"/media/eec4812ff383feae5151d806a7dd0364ad33ace1.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and \u0001<img src=\"/media/2daee51acaceb45eaa0f24ed14beb658ee4e2dea.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then what is the value of <img src=\"/media/8e1f0e666bec4911b04a0228c10d7c81d78ca94c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u0001 is _________.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4, 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 8, 12</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 7, 14</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/170bcd060e933d8324108f3abb9b05291bdd531f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/501a7a602e830cc78cdef7aefbf40437d4739e95.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A vector <em>V</em> = (2, 1, –1)<sup>T</sup> lies in R3.<br />\nConsider the plane defined by the equation <em>x</em> – y + z = 0.<br />\nWhich of the following represents the orthogonal projection of <em>v</em> onto the plane?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The vector lies on the plane, so it’s projection is (2, 1, –1)<em><sup>T</sup></em>.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The projection lies on the plan and is orthogonal to the normal vector (0, –1, 1)<sup>T</sup>.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The projection is obtained by subtracting the component of <em>V</em> a long the normal from <em>V</em> itself.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The projection is a scalar multiple of vector (1, –1, 1)<em><sup>T</sup></em>.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f9c6989257cec0f7a8320dc88fb8e92c62d20050.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":16,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:08.431Z"}